source: tests/stages.rs
expression: reports.report(path)
input_file: tests/fixtures/expand/doc_syntax_pages.rslisp
---
(def thread-page "(->> value form ...)\n\nThreads a value through each form as its last argument.\n\n`(->> 3 (- 10) (* 2))` is `(* 2 (- 10 3))`. A bare name in place of a form\nis called with the value alone.")
(def the-page "(the type value)\n\nGives a value a written type.\n\nIt binds the value with an annotated `let` and returns it, so a literal is\nchecked against the type and a value that is not `copy` moves. A value of\nanother type is an error, except that a borrowed `string`, `(ref name)`,\npasses as a `(ref str)`.")
(def loop-page "(loop (name value ...) body ...)\n\nBinds names to values and runs a body that `recur` repeats.\n\nThe list is the binding list of `let`, so each value sees the names bound\nbefore it. A name given twice is an error, because `recur` passes one value\nper name.\n\n`(recur new-value ...)` in tail position runs the body again with each name\nbound to its new value. The call returns the body's last value.\n\nThe body is a function, so `try`, `let-try` and `try->` in it leave the loop\nwith the failure, not the enclosing function.")
(def let-try-page "(let-try (name value ...) body ...)\n\nBinds each name to the value inside a `result` or an `option`, in order.\n\nThe list is the binding list of `let`.\n\nEach value goes through `try`, so the first `err` or `none` returns from the\nenclosing function, or leaves the enclosing `loop`. That function must\nreturn a `result` or an `option` of the same kind.")
(def try-thread-page "(try-> value function ...)\n\nCalls each function on the result of the one before, through `try`.\n\n`(try-> x f g)` is `(g (try (f x)))`, so the first `err` or `none` returns\nfrom the enclosing function, or leaves the enclosing `loop`, and the last\nresult is returned as it is. With no function, the call returns the value.\n\nUnlike `->`, a step takes no extra arguments: a call form is a call whose\nresult is the function, so `(try-> x (make-step))` is `((make-step) x)`.")
(def comment-page "(comment form ...)\n\nKeeps forms in the source that never expand, check or run.\n\nThe call is unit, so a file can hold scratch expressions to evaluate one at\na time from an editor.")
